text:
Pasal 8

1. Pemerintah Daerah melakukan upaya pencegahan  kekerasan, eksploitasi dan diskriminasi terhadap  perempuan secara terpadu di Daerah.
2. Pencegahan kekerasan, eksploitasi dan diskriminasi terhadap perempuan dimaksudkan untuk menciptakan  lingkungan yang aman bagi perempuan dan untuk  mengurangi kerentanan kekerasan, eksploitasi dan  diskriminasi kepada kelompok perempuan rentan.
3. Kelompok Perempuan rentan sebagaimana dimaksud  pada ayat (2) meliputi:
a. perempuan dalam situasi bencana dan konflik  sosial;
b. perempuan dengan penyandang disabilitas;
c. perempuan dengan HIV/AIDS;
d. perempuan pekerja migran;
e. perempuan kepala keluarga;
f. perempuan pekerja rumah tangga;
g. perempuan pekerja rumahan;
h. perempuan lanjut usia;
i. perempuan pekerja informal;
j. perempuan dalam situasi intoleransi; dan
k. kelompok perempuan rentan lainnya.
4. Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dan ayat (2) dilaksanakan dengan cara:
a. melakukan koordinasi, integrasi, sinkronisasi  pencegahan tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi dan  diskriminasi berdasarkan pola kemitraan;
b. melakukan sosialisasi mengenai peraturan  perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan  pelindungan hak perempuan;
c. membangun dan menyediakan sistem informasi  pencegahan kekerasan, eksploitasi dan  diskriminasi yang lengkap dan mudah diakses;
d. memberikan kemudahan akses untuk memperoleh  hak sipil, pendidikan, kesehatan, ketenagakerjaan,  pelatihan dan pendanaan, peningkatan  kesejahteraan dan pelayanan;
e. mengembangkan media komunikasi, informasi,  edukasi dan kampanye publik melalui media;
f. mengembangkan materi dan kurikulum  pendidikan;
g. mengembangkan sistem transportasi dan ruang  publik yang aman;
h. membangun sistem deteksi dini, keamanan dan  layanan pengaduan terpadu di kawasan industri,  perusahaan, lingkungan pemukiman, lingkungan  pendidikan, pesantren dan ruang publik lainnya;
i. memberikan layanan konsultasi bagi keluarga,  calon pengantin, pelajar, santri, pemuda, mahasiswa dan kelompok rentan;
j. mendorong perubahan perilaku orang tua dan  masyarakat;
k. mengembangkan kebijakan terkait  kabupaten/kota, kelurahan, sekolah, pesantren,  dan perguruan tinggi yang aman dan ramah bagi  perempuan dan terintegrasi dengan kebijakan tata  ruang wilayah;
l. membentuk dan mengembangkan kader,  komunitas, dan kelompok dari kalangan muda,  pelajar, santri, mahasiswa, jurnalis, influencer media sosial, tenaga pendidik, dan tokoh agama  untuk pencegahan;
m. melakukan edukasi dan advokasi kepada pemilik,  pengelola dan/atau pengguna sosial media;
n. mengembangkan sistem pelindungan dan  dukungan khusus bagi kelompok perempuan  rentan;
o. melakukan penyadaran bagi pelaku;
p. meningkatkan kapasitas Perangkat Daerah,  instansi pemerintah, lembaga pendidikan, lembaga  keagamaan, Lembaga penyelenggara pelayanan  kesehatan, lembaga profesi, dunia usaha, lembaga  layanan, pesantren, organisasi kepemudaan,  organisasi bantuan hukum, media, tokoh agama,  tokoh masyarakat dan komunitas; dan
q. membentuk jaringan kerjasama dalam upaya  pencegahan dari tindak kekerasan, eksploitasi dan  diskriminasi dengan aparatur penegak hukum,  instansi pemerintah, Perangkat Daerah, lembaga  masyarakat, lembaga pendidikan, tokoh  masyarakat, lembaga keagamaan, Lembaga  penyelenggara pelayanan kesehatan, lembaga  profesi, dunia usaha, lembaga layanan, pesantren,  organisasi kepemudaan, organisasi bantuan  hukum, komunitas, dan media.
5. Upaya pencegahan Kekerasan, Eksploitasi dan  Diskriminasi terhadap perempuan secara terpadu  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dikoordinasikan  oleh Perangkat Daerah yang menyelenggarakan urusan  pemerintahan di bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan  pelindungan anak serta urusan pemerintahan bidang  pengendalian penduduk dan keluarga berencana.
6. Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (3) huruf a dapat melibatkan Perangkat Daerah,  instansi, lembaga masyarakat, lembaga pendidikan,  tokoh masyarakat, pos pelayanan terpadu, pusat  pembelajaran keluarga, lembaga keagamaan, lembaga  penyelenggara pelayanan kesehatan, lembaga profesi,  dunia usaha, lembaga layanan, pesantren, organisasi kepemudaan, organisasi bantuan hukum, komunitas,  dan media.

translated_text:
Article 8

1. The Regional Government undertakes efforts to prevent violence, exploitation and discrimination against women in an integrated manner in the Region.
2. The prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women is intended to create a safe environment for women and to reduce the vulnerability to violence, exploitation and discrimination of vulnerable groups of women.
3. Vulnerable groups of women as referred to in paragraph (2) include:
a. women in disaster and social conflict situations;
b. women with disabilities;
c. women with HIV/AIDS;
d. women migrant workers;
e. women heads of households;
f. domestic workers;
g. home-based workers;
h. elderly women;
i. informal sector workers;
j. women in situations of intolerance; and
k. other vulnerable groups of women.
4. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are implemented by:
a. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of the prevention of acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination based on partnership patterns;
b. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women's rights;
c. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system for the prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination;
d. providing ease of access to obtain civil rights, education, health, employment, training and funding, welfare improvement and services;
e. developing communication media, information, education and public campaigns through media;
f. developing educational materials and curricula;
g. developing safe transportation systems and public spaces;
h. building early detection systems, security and integrated complaint services in industrial areas, companies, residential areas, educational environments, Islamic boarding schools and other public spaces;
i. providing consultation services for families, prospective brides and grooms, students, Islamic boarding school students, youth, university students and vulnerable groups;
j. encouraging behavioral change of parents and the community;
k. developing policies related to regencies/cities, sub-districts, schools, Islamic boarding schools, and universities that are safe and friendly for women and integrated with regional spatial planning policies;
l. forming and developing cadres, communities, and groups from among youth, students, Islamic boarding school students, university students, journalists, social media influencers, educators, and religious leaders for prevention;
m. conducting education and advocacy to owners, managers and/or users of social media;
n. developing protection systems and special support for vulnerable groups of women;
o. conducting awareness-raising for perpetrators;
p. increasing the capacity of Regional Apparatus, government agencies, educational institutions, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, the business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, media, religious leaders, community leaders and communities; and
q. forming cooperation networks in prevention efforts against acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination with law enforcement apparatus, government agencies, Regional Apparatus, community institutions, educational institutions, community leaders, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, the business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, communities, and media.
5. Efforts to prevent Violence, Exploitation and Discrimination against women in an integrated manner as referred to in paragraph (1) are coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection as well as governmental affairs in the field of population control and family planning.
6. Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (3) letter a may involve Regional Apparatus, agencies, community institutions, educational institutions, community leaders, integrated service posts, family learning centers, religious institutions, health service provider institutions, professional institutions, the business sector, service institutions, Islamic boarding schools, youth organizations, legal aid organizations, communities, and media.

